# Tutorial examples that need a compiler NEWER than the released one,
# by name, with the version they wait for and why.  tutrelease.sh
# excuses exactly these, while that version is the one this tree is
# building and is not yet published -- and never on main.
#
#   NAME  VERSION   why
#
# A line here is a promise with a date on it: the release that
# carries the version removes it (the pointer commit), and
# tutrelease fails on a line whose version is out, whose example
# agrees with the release after all, or whose example is gone.
C6Nan      0.29.0   interpolation literals
C8Zarr     0.29.0   interpolation literals
C10Icos    0.29.0   interpolation literals
C12Pad     0.29.0   interpolation literals
C12Line    0.29.0   the interpolation literal is its subject
C13Kinds   0.29.0   interpolation literals
C13Modes   0.29.0   interpolation literals
C14Flux    0.29.0   interpolation literals
C15Stats   0.29.0   interpolation literals
C16Hash    0.29.0   interpolation literals
C16Mat     0.29.0   interpolation literals
C17Pipe    0.29.0   interpolation literals, a slice in brackets, a character beside a BYTE
C18Dist    0.29.0   interpolation literals, a CONST over CONSTs
C18Fit     0.29.0   interpolation literals
C18Taylor  0.29.0   interpolation literals
X12Hole    0.29.0   the refusal of a hole's format
